.TH TINTFETCH 1 "November 2026" "Tintfetch" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tintfetch \- display system information and colorful distribution artwork
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tintfetch
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tintfetch is a native Go system information utility with
HyFetch color profiles and fastfetch-style information modules.
Unavailable optional information is omitted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show the complete native and HyFetch-compatible option list.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version.
.TP
.B --config PATH
Select an info configuration file; command options override its settings.
.TP
.BR --no_config ", " --no-config
Ignore info configuration files. HyFetch JSON configuration is independent.
.TP
.BR --print_config ", " --print-config
Print the default info configuration.
.TP
.BR --stdout ", " --plain
Print plain text without artwork or ANSI styling.
.TP
.B --json
Print an object containing version and result. Result rows have key,
optional label, and value string fields.
.TP
.BR --list_modules
List information modules.
.TP
.B --structure MODULES
Choose a colon-separated module list, or all. Some modules run commands or
make network requests when explicitly selected.
.TP
.BR -p ", " --preset " NAME"
Choose a native HyFetch color preset.
.TP
.B -c
Interactively configure HyFetch color options.
.TP
.B -C PATH
Select a HyFetch JSON configuration.
.TP
.B --shell-config
Execute a trusted Bash configuration selected with an explicit --config PATH.
This grants the file the user's permissions. Only info calls are collected
from its print_info function. Ordinary info configuration is not sourced.
.TP
.B --source PATH
Select artwork. Image rendering uses optional external tools when installed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tintfetch/config.conf
Native user configuration; the OS user config directory is used otherwise.
.TP
.I /etc/tintfetch/config.conf
System configuration. Neofetch paths remain fallbacks.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hyfetch.json
HyFetch-compatible color configuration.
.SH NOTES
Some image compatibility options remain placeholders. Consult the installed
compatibility document and --help for the implemented behavior.
.SH AUTHORS
Tintfetch contributors; derived in part from Neofetch and HyFetch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR neofetch (1),
.BR hyfetch (1),
.BR fastfetch (1)
